{{PageBanner|Eve_l_184_en.png|event}}
'''Ranking Dojo''' (ネコ道場ランキングイベント, ''Neko Dōjō Rankingu Ibento'', '''Cat Dojo Ranking Event''') is an event that first appeared from July 31st to August 7th, 2017. This event was officially added in the [[Version 6.3 Update]]. The Ranking Dojo is accessed from the [[Catclaw Dojo]] menu, so the player needs to unlock the Catclaw Dojo feature in order to participate by completing Chapter 1 of [[Empire of Cats]].

==About Ranking Dojo==
During this event, the cat on the front door is replaced with the ranking as shown below. A new, blue-colored Dojo area is available aside [[Wanderer's Trial (Stage 1)|Hall of Initiates]]. On the right from top to bottom are the Rewards List button, the Ranking Chart and personal statistics including personal high score, personal ranking in percentage and personal title: [[File:Ranking Dojo.png|center|600px|Initial ranking]]

==About Ranking Dojo Battles==
The player has 3 instead of the usual 5 minutes limit during an Arena of Honor stage. These stages require 30 [[Cat Energy|Energy]] to play. If the player exits the game during the battle, Energy won't be refunded. Other than that, stage's gimmick is same as regular Dojo Stages:
*The player has an unlimited supply of [[Battle Items#Speed Up|Speed Ups]] and [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPUs]], other items are disabled.
*The player's score increases as their cats defeat enemies.
*Defeating enemies won't give money.
*After 3 minutes, remaining enemies on screen are not wiped, nothing happens even if they knockout the [[Cat Base]].
*The enemy base is an indestructible [[Dummy (Enemy Base)|Dummy]].
*Score per enemy kill = Enemy's Cash Drop [unaffected by treasures or abilities] + Enemy's Dojo Bounty Score [Refer to the respective dojo's schematics] * (1 + Current Dojo Time Left[seconds] / Total Dojo Time[seconds])
[[File:Ranking Dojo 2.png|600px|center]]
After clearing a Ranking Stage, the player will be given a title depend on the score, this requires Internet connection to update the ranking.
[[File:Ranking Dojo 3.png|center|600px]]

==Rewards List==
Depends on personal ranking in percentage, the player will be given a title and receive rewards sent to their mailbox found in the [[Main Menu]].

When the first three Ranking Dojos were released, all rankings gave the player much less [[Cat Food]]. This was later changed to compensate the players' effort in the rankings.

